# .dockerignore — repo-root build context ignore file. Primary gate for
# `docker build -f agent/Dockerfile .` (repo root is the documented build
# context — see agent/Dockerfile's header comment). agent/.dockerignore is
# a defence-in-depth duplicate for the (undocumented, unused) case of
# building with ./agent as the context directly.
#
# node_modules is the critical entry here: without it, `COPY agent ./agent`
# and `COPY packages/shared ./packages/shared` pull in the HOST's own
# locally-installed node_modules (host-OS-specific symlinks — e.g. absolute
# Windows paths on a Windows dev box) on top of the image's own, correct,
# freshly `pnpm install`-ed node_modules from the builder stage, silently
# breaking module resolution at runtime (the build itself still exits 0).

node_modules
dist
*.tsbuildinfo
.vitest-cache
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store
.git
tests/
**/*.test.ts
